  "title": "Ellen Johnson Sirleaf",
  "summary": "Ellen Johnson Sirleaf, born in Monrovia in 1938, won Liberia's 2005 presidential election and was inaugurated on 16 January 2006 as the 24th president, the first elected woman head of state in Africa. She shared the 2011 Nobel Peace Prize and was re-elected that year.",
